{"1096200": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "The Orville - Interactive Fan Experience", "steam_appid": 1096200, "required_age": 0, "is_free": true, "detailed_description": "Step aboard the <strong>USS Orville</strong> (ECV-197), the Planetary Union's finest mid-level exploratory class cruiser. With every room on every deck recreated with painstaking accuracy you are free to explore the weirdest ship in the fleet at your leisure, either alone or with friends in multiplayer. <br><br><strong>Current Features:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Freely explore the ship in both first and third person.<br></li><li> Sit at the helm and take the ship for a spin. Why not try and see if you too can &quot;hug the donkey&quot;?<br></li><li> Jump into multiplayer with a few friends and explore the ship together. Alternatively you can pick up a Longbow and test out your marksmanship on them. <br></li><li> Visit the E-Sim and go bowling, or visit Bortus' &quot;special&quot; program, if you can find it!<br></li><li> Character customisation. Be who you want to be! <br></li><li> Synthesise a few nick-knacks at any of the ship's matter synthesizers. Pick them up and place them freely. Why not give Bortus and Clyden's quarters a quick spruce up?<br></li><li> Take in the breathtaking views out of the Mess Hall windows of the Planetary Union Dockyard in Earth orbit.<br></li><li> Customize your own quarters and upload it to the Steam Workshop for everyone to marvel at!<br></li><li> Send the ship into disarray with a variety of different alert modes, each changing the ambiance throughout the ship. Find the one that best suits your mood. Or perhaps you've just got the urge to party like a Moclan?<br></li><li> Completely original score with undertones and themes from the show by the legendary Patrick Phillips.<br></li><li> In-game chat for both text and voice in Multiplayer games. All in aid of the great Orville community spirit.<br></li><li> Wander down to the Shuttle Bay and take a shuttle out for a joyride.<br></li><li> Fight Kaylon ships in the Unknown Sector.</li></ul>", "about_the_game": "Step aboard the <strong>USS Orville</strong> (ECV-197), the Planetary Union's finest mid-level exploratory class cruiser. With every room on every deck recreated with painstaking accuracy you are free to explore the weirdest ship in the fleet at your leisure, either alone or with friends in multiplayer. <br><br><strong>Current Features:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Freely explore the ship in both first and third person.<br></li><li> Sit at the helm and take the ship for a spin. Why not try and see if you too can &quot;hug the donkey&quot;?<br></li><li> Jump into multiplayer with a few friends and explore the ship together. Alternatively you can pick up a Longbow and test out your marksmanship on them. <br></li><li> Visit the E-Sim and go bowling, or visit Bortus' &quot;special&quot; program, if you can find it!<br></li><li> Character customisation. Be who you want to be! <br></li><li> Synthesise a few nick-knacks at any of the ship's matter synthesizers. Pick them up and place them freely. Why not give Bortus and Clyden's quarters a quick spruce up?<br></li><li> Take in the breathtaking views out of the Mess Hall windows of the Planetary Union Dockyard in Earth orbit.<br></li><li> Customize your own quarters and upload it to the Steam Workshop for everyone to marvel at!<br></li><li> Send the ship into disarray with a variety of different alert modes, each changing the ambiance throughout the ship. Find the one that best suits your mood. Or perhaps you've just got the urge to party like a Moclan?<br></li><li> Completely original score with undertones and themes from the show by the legendary Patrick Phillips.<br></li><li> In-game chat for both text and voice in Multiplayer games. All in aid of the great Orville community spirit.<br></li><li> Wander down to the Shuttle Bay and take a shuttle out for a joyride.<br></li><li> Fight Kaylon ships in the Unknown Sector.</li></ul>", "short_description": "Step aboard the USS Orville (ECV-197), the Planetary Union's finest mid-level exploratory class cruiser. With every room on every deck recreated with painstaking accuracy, you are free to explore the ship at your leisure and engage in all manner of shenanigans!", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong>, French, German, Czech, Hungarian, Portuguese - Brazil, Spanish - Spain, Simplified Chinese<br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1096200/e698488dd80679717c208d9195480288c165295d/header.jpg?t=1785223168", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1096200/89f031071ea42682e3f85808ab7f5a002344a285/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1785223168", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1096200/89f031071ea42682e3f85808ab7f5a002344a285/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1785223168", "website": "http://www.orvillefangame.co.uk", "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel i5<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 8 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> Nvidia 1080 Ti<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 11<br></li><li><strong>Network:</strong> Broadband Internet connection<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 10 GB available space<br></li><li><strong>Sound Card:</strong> Integrated Audio<br></li><li><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> SSD or NVMe Recommended</li></ul>", "recommended": "<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel i7<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 16 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Grap